# ====================================================================
# CNG-Connect environment variables.
# Copy to .env.local for local dev, or set in your Vercel project's
# Environment Variables (Production/Preview/Development).
# ====================================================================

# --- Supabase backend + auth (required) ---
# Without these, the app falls back to per-device localStorage: no driver
# ever sees another driver's reports/comments/posts, and sign-in doesn't
# work at all (auth is real Supabase Auth now, not a custom system).
# Create a free project at https://supabase.com, then:
#   1. Run supabase/schema.sql in the SQL Editor.
#   2. Copy the Project URL and anon/public key from Settings > API.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="YOUR_ANON_PUBLIC_KEY"

# Service-role key (Settings > API > service_role). SERVER-ONLY — never
# prefix this with VITE_ or it will be bundled into the client. Not used by
# the app's own serverless functions today, but keep it out of client code
# if you add any admin-only endpoints later (e.g. approving station
# suggestions, moderating content).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="YOUR_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY"

# --- Email sign-in (Supabase Auth email OTP) — free, no SMS costs ---
# Sign-in/sign-up is a single email + 6-digit-code flow (no password),
# handled entirely by Supabase Auth (supabase.auth.signInWithOtp /
# verifyOtp) — there is no app-level OTP env var to set. Two things need
# configuring in the Supabase dashboard for it to actually deliver:
#
#   1. Authentication > Providers > Email — enable the Email provider if
#      it isn't already.
#   2. Authentication > Emails > SMTP Settings — enable Custom SMTP so you
#      aren't limited to Supabase's shared sender (a handful of emails/hour,
#      "for testing" per their own docs). Point it at Resend's SMTP relay:
#        Host: smtp.resend.com   Port: 465 (or 587)
#        Username: resend
#        Password: your Resend API key (https://resend.com — free tier,
#                   100/day, 3,000/month, no domain verification needed)
#        Sender email: any address (e.g. onboarding@resend.dev works)
#   3. Authentication > Emails > Email Templates > "Magic Link" — by
#      default this template links to a URL. Edit it to reference
#      {{ .Token }} instead (Supabase's docs call this out explicitly) so
#      the email contains a 6-digit code, which is what the sign-in screen
#      asks the driver to type — without this edit, drivers get a link with
#      nothing to type in.

# --- AI Assistant (optional) ---
# Required for the in-app AI Assistant (api/chat.ts). Without it, that
# feature returns a clean error instead of a response.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# APP_URL: The URL where this app is hosted (self-referential links, etc).
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"
